✅ Iterator
Used to traverse elements in a collection.
Methods:
hasNext() → Checks if more elements exist.
next() → Returns next element.
remove() → Removes current element.

✅ Collection Framework
Provides javainterfaces and classes for storing and manipulating groups of objects.
Located in java.util package.
Main Interfaces:
Collection → Root interface.
z


✅ Hierarchy
Collection Interface
List → ArrayList, LinkedList, Vector
Set → HashSet, LinkedHashSet, TreeSet
Queue → PriorityQueue, Deque

Map Interface
HashMap, LinkedHashMap, TreeMap, Hashtable

✅ Key Points
ArrayList → Dynamic array.
LinkedList → Doubly linked list.
HashSet → Unordered set.
TreeSet → Sorted set.
HashMap → Key-value pairs, unordered.
TreeMap → Sorted key-value pairs.
